<title>NEW ZEALAND: RBNZ says Brash not publishing book.</title>
<headline>RBNZ says Brash not publishing book.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand on Monday denied media reports that Governor Don Brash had published a book entitled &quot;New Zealand's Remarkable Reforms&quot;.</p>
<p>The title belonged to a speech given by Brash to the British Institute of Economic Affairs last June, and now published by the institute in booklet form, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
